  "body": "I am reading the values of my HR device through Web Bluethooth.\r\n\r\nThis is an example of read values:\r\n\r\n```\r\n0x10 0x3e 0xb1 0x3 0xde\r\n0x10 0x39 0x23 0x4 0x35\r\n0x10 0x3d 0xcf 0x3 0xef\r\n```\r\nI convert these numbers into decimal numbers and I have:\r\n\r\n```\r\n16 62 177 3 222\r\n16 57 35 4 53\r\n16 61 207 3 239\r\n```\r\nWhere:\r\n\r\n- The second column represents the heart beats per minute (62 - 57 - 61).\r\n- The fourth column represents the RR interval (222 - 53 - 239).\r\n\r\nBut the numbers seem wrong to me. \r\nIf I have beats around 60 per minute, I should have a higher RR interval than the value I read.\r\n\r\nDo I make any conversion errors? Is the RR value to be read in another way?",
